completed_at: "2026-08-04T16:11:15.217Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 900
acceptance_criteria: "A filed item can declare a machine-readable population measurement carrying selector, count, and owning item, so the number in the description and the number a gate enforces are the same number; A check recomputes every declared population from tracked data and fails when an observed count exceeds its declared ceiling, naming the item, selector, declared count, observed count, and the mutations that added the difference; The check runs identically in the local pre-push gate set and in hosted CI, and drift between the two selected sets fails; Closing an owning item retires its ceiling, so no ceiling outlives the defect it guards and no waiver is needed to close honest work; The two populations proved here are declared first: pm-jkbqt8 blocks rows at 241 and pm-4020c5 related_to rows at 43, each recording the growth already observed since it was measured; A negative control proves the check can fail: adding one row beyond a declared ceiling in a sandbox tracker turns the gate red, and the fixture is registered in the gate registry alongside the existing tracker-integrity control"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "pm 2026.8.3 tracker at HEAD, census over all 2301 tracked item files"
resolution: "Implemented a checked-in, owner-linked, shrinking-only measurement registry and fail-closed evaluator covering dependency aliases, graph quality, every live validator warning class, and health severities; local and hosted gates now reject regressions and undeclared populations."
expected_result: "A filed measurement is executable context: any population increase or new unowned validator or health class fails locally and in CI with owner and mutation attribution."
actual_result: "Nineteen live measurements are enforced across 2314 items; update mode cannot widen ceilings, terminal owners retire declarations, negative control fails on one added blocks row, and local, CI-contract, packed npm/npx, and Bun acceptance paths pass."
